    { q: 'The Bellman equation expresses the idea that…', choices: ['rewards must be positive', 'the value of a state is its immediate reward plus the discounted value of the best next state', 'all states are equal', 'exploration is always better'], answer: 1, why: 'V(s) = r + γ·V(s′) — a recursive definition of "how good is being here", which turns long-horizon planning into repeated one-step bootstrapping.' },
